{
  "stem": "advanced_shipping_2022_W43_ADVANCED-MARKET-REPORT-WEEK-43",
  "source_file": "advanced_shipping_2022_W43_ADVANCED-MARKET-REPORT-WEEK-43.pdf",
  "issue_date": "2022-10-27",
  "report_week": "43",
  "report_period": "Week 43 (21st Oct to 27th Oct 2022)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "The Post Panamax \"Pellonia\" 93/2010 Jiangsu, China (SS/DD 03/2025) was committed to undisclosed buyers for USD 17,2 mill. Remind you that the sister vessels \"Jin Lang\" & \"Jin Mei\" 93/2010 Jiangsu, China (SS 04/2025, DD 04/2023 & SS 03/2025, DD 04/2023 respectively) were sold a week ago at USD 17,25 mill each. China Minsheng Trust have sold their two Kamsarmax \"CCS Orchid\" 82/2017 Jiangsu, China (SS 01/2027, DD 02/2025, BWTS fitted) & \"MSXT Hera\" 81/2018 Chengxi, China (SS/DD 11/2023, BWTS fitted) to Chinese buyers for USD 54 mill enbloc. Note that back in September, the younger \"Nord Corona\" 81/2019 Jiangsu, China (SS 09/2024, DD 09/2022, BWTS fitted) was sold for USD 29 mill. Pan Ocean have committed their Panamax \"Pan Diva\" 76/2004 Sasebo, Japan (SS 09/2024, DD 06/2024, BWTS fitted) for low USD 13 mill. Furthermore, Apollonia Lines sold their \"Blue Chip\" 76/2007 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 11/2022) to Korean buyers for low USD 15 mill, while the one-year- older \"Seawind\" 75/2006 Sanoyas, Japan (SS 05/2026, DD 09/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold for USD 15,2 mill. For reference, the \"Bellatrix\" 77/2006 Oshima, Japan (SS 02/2026, DD 08/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold a couple of weeks ago at USD 14,6 mill. The Ultramax \"Van Star\" 61/2011 Shin Kasado, Japan (SS 12/2025, DD 12/2023, BWTS fitted) was sold to undisclosed buyers for high USD 21 mill, while the \"Ultra Wollongong\" 61/2011 Oshima, Japan (SS 06/2026, DD 06/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold a week ago at USD 22 mill. On the Handysize sector, Japanese owners sold their \"Belle Ocean\" 28/2014 I-S, Japan (SS/DD 03/2024, BWTS fitted) to Greek buyers for region USD 15 mill. Remind you that the one-year-older sister vessel \"Malto Hope\" 28/2013 I-S, Japan (SS/DD 07/2023, BWTS fitted) was sold in September at USD 13,6 mill.",
    "tankers": "Eurotankers have committed their Suezmax \"Euroglory\" 166/2005 Brodosplit, Croatia (SS 04/2025, DD 01/2024) for USD 26 mill. For reference, the two-years-older Chinese built \"Da Ming Hu\" 159/2003 Bohai, China (SS/DD 11/2023, BWTS fitted) was sold a week ago at USD 22 mill. Following the sale of the MR2 \"Gotland Carolina\" 53/2006 Guangzhou, China (SS 12/2026, DD 03/2025, BWTS fitted, Ice Class 1A Super) a couple of months ago, Gotland Rederi have now sold the sister vessels \"Gotland Sofia\" 53/2007 Guangzhou, China (SS 03/2027, DD 05/2025, BWTS fitted, Ice Class 1A Super) for USD 18 mill and the one-year-younger \"Gotland Aliya\" (SS/DD 07/2023, Ice Class 1A Super) & \"Gotland Marieann\" 53/2008 Guangzhou, China (SS/DD 08/2023, BWTS fitted, Ice Class 1A Super) for USD 18,5 mill each to Chinese buyers.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of mid usd 8,00's fio range. A number of round trips on the same route were reported in the usd 12,000/13,000 pd range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 14,000/16,000 pd range. Australian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 18,000/20,000 pd. Indian trips via East Coast South America into China were fixed around usd 15,000/17,000 pd. Indian trips via South Africa into Mediterranean were reported at the level of usd 15,000 pd. Inter- continental trips via North Coast South America were fixed around usd 17,000/19,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Continent were reported at the level of usd 20,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 200K. On the period front, Kamsarmax was reported fixed at the level of usd 17,000 pd for 6/8 months employment basis delivery China.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 13,000/15,000 pd range. West Coast Indian trips into East Coast India were fixed around usd 19,000/21,000 pd. Continental trips into China were reported at the level of usd 25,000/27,000 pd. Trips from US East Coast via East Coast South America into Caribbean were fixed around usd 17,000/19,000 pd. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Trips from China into Southeast Asia were reported at the level of usd 10,000/12,000 pd. Australian trips into China with concentrates were reported fixed in the usd 14,000/16,000 pd range. Mediterranean trips into US Gulf were fixed around usd 21,000/23,000 pd. Mediterranean trips into Continent were reported at the level of usd 21,000/22,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
